# Environment Variables

This file contains environment variables needed for the application.
Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your actual values.

## Required Variables

```bash
# Groq API Key
# Get your key from: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key-here
```

## Optional Variables

```bash
# Vector Database (if using Qdrant)
QDRANT_HOST=localhost
QDRANT_PORT=6333

# Database Connection (if using database MCP)
DATABASE_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/mydb
DATABASE_USER=your-username
DATABASE_PASSWORD=your-password
```

## Usage

### Linux/Mac
```bash
export GROQ_API_KEY=your-actual-key-here
mvn spring-boot:run
```

### Windows (PowerShell)
```powershell
$env:GROQ_API_KEY="your-actual-key-here"
mvn spring-boot:run
```

### Using .env file (with spring-boot-dotenv)
```bash
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your actual values
mvn spring-boot:run
```
